    "notes": "Q804210 and OSM way 230401645 identify Bayterek. The star-shaped footprint controls the lattice feet, the independently mapped globe controls the sphere diameter and the two mapped stair lines control signed heading. The modeled 97 m observation level and 105 m mast height are distinct. The two mapped building height tags are retained as source evidence. Standard terrain and exterior photographs determine the reconstructed plinth and branch proportions. The sphere uses reflective opaque panels and modeled seams. The visitor interiors, fountain animation and independent landscape fixtures remain outside the landmark model. The generic pedestrian surface still overlaps the center of the lowest east treads in the standard terrain capture. Physical-device timings are unmeasured."
  },
